        1650,
        1700
      ],
      "category": "Text",
      "text": "In the event that the parties are unable to reach agreement as to substantive terms and conditions of employment after sincere and exhaustive bargaining, they may seek the intervention of the Commissioner of Labor or, if the public interest so requires, the Commissioner of Labor may profit for his services upon his own motion. It shall thereupon be the duty of the Commissioner of Labor to take such steps as he may deem expedient to effect an expeditious adjustment and settlement of the differences between the parties.",
