        1622,
        2181
      ],
      "category": "Text",
      "text": "Until a majority representative has been selected for the purposes of bargaining collectively for a particular employee grouping or unit, any labor organization having members among the employees in such grouping or unit may represent such members for the purposes and in the manner and under the conditions set forth in section 6 of the Interim Order of July 21, 1954, as amended on March 14, 1955, dealing with the establishment of and participation in joint labor relations committees. The provisions of section 6 of the Interim Order, as amended, are hereby incorporated in and made a part of this order to the extent herein indicated.",
